      "text": "The Alps are a major mountain system in south-central Europe, curving in a broad arc from the Ligurian Sea and southeastern France eastward toward Slovenia and the Adriatic. The Alpine Convention identifies an Alpine region spanning eight countries: Austria, France, Germany, Italy, Liechtenstein, Monaco, Slovenia, and Switzerland. The range is distinguished by high, rugged folded mountains, including Mont Blanc, and by its importance as a source area for major rivers such as the Rhine, Rhône, and Po. The Alps formed through tectonic compression and uplift associated with the collision of the Adriatic microplate and Eurasian Plate; mountain passes have long connected northern and Mediterranean Europe.",
